{
	"about": [
		"Exchanges. A session is new, or authenticated as device \"d1\" of app \"todo\". With the backend in the state given, a client call sends the client frame (and clientBody, if any); the server answers with the server frames (and serverBody); the call resolves with result or fails with the error code. push is a changed frame the server sends unasked.",
		"closes: the server closes the channel after its frames. An error frame also carries a message, English text for a developer whose wording is the server's; it is not compared.",
		"Bodies are UTF-8 text. backend keys: welcome, helloError, paired, pairError, head, doc, put ({stored} or {conflict}), putError.",
		"tolerated: frames one side accepts although the other side never sends them."
	],
